+/**
+ * NODE MODEL — explicit internal boundary (barrel)
+ *
+ * This module defines the public surface of the n8n **Node Model** LEGO:
+ *
+ *   - Node definition      (INodeType, IVersionedNodeType, abstract Node)
+ *   - Node identity        (INode, INodes, INodeCredentials[Details], OnError)
+ *   - Node type/version    (INodeTypeDescription, INodeTypeBaseDescription, VersionedNodeType)
+ *   - Node parameters      (INodeProperties and sub-types, INodeParameters, NodeParameterValueType)
+ *   - Node inputs/outputs  (NodeConnectionTypes, INodeInputConfiguration, INodeOutputConfiguration)
+ *   - Node metadata/issues (INodeIssues, NodeHint, NodeExecutionHint, icons/codex)
+ *   - Node configuration   (IDisplayOptions, display conditions, credentials-in-description)
+ *   - Node lifecycle API   (execute/supplyData/trigger/poll/webhook/methods/webhookMethods/customOperations)
+ *
+ * It is a NON-BREAKING boundary: nothing was moved. All symbols are re-exported
+ * from their original modules (`interfaces`, `node-helpers`, `versioned-node-type`,
+ * `node-validation`, `node-parameters/*`). Existing imports via `n8n-workflow`
+ * keep working verbatim; the package `index.ts` keeps `export *` of everything.
+ *
+ * Deliberately NOT exported here (owned by other subsystems):
+ *   - Credentials model   (ICredentialType, ICredentialsHelper, ...)        → credentials
+ *   - Execution runtime   (IRun, IRunData, ITaskData, run-execution-data)   → execution (Agent 3)
+ *   - Workflow graph      (Workflow class, IWorkflowBase, connections-diff) → workflow (Agent 1)
+ *   - Expression runtime  (expression evaluator, workflow-data-proxy)       → expression
+ *   - NodeTypes registry implementation, LoadNodesAndCredentials            → cli/loading (Agent 4)
+ *   - RoutingNode / node execution contexts (runtime side)                  → core (Agent 3)
+ *
+ * See contracts/node.contract.md and docs/isolation/node.md.
+ */
+
